<header class="resume-heading"><h1>Conor Brown</h1><p><strong>Software Engineer · C#/.NET · Claude Code & Agent Engineering</strong></p><p>Oklahoma, USA · <a href="mailto:carllbrown87@gmail.com">carllbrown87@gmail.com</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/conor--brown/">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://github.com/conorbrown-dev">GitHub</a></p></header>
<section><h2>Professional summary</h2><p>Software engineer with 12+ years of professional .NET experience and ownership of design and delivery across operational applications, payment services, and distributed infrastructure. Daily AI-assisted development experience with Claude Code and Codex, including building an agent harness used daily by teammates. Combines C#/ASP.NET Core, SQL Server, Azure, testing, performance tuning, and legacy modernization with architecture reviews, mentoring, and practical AI development conventions.</p></section>
<section><h2>AI engineering &amp; selected impact</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Built Mega Desk, an agent harness used daily by teammates:</strong> integrates Claude Agent SDK and Codex CLI with Azure DevOps work-item prioritization, implementation handoff, PR reviews, comment resolution, and merge-conflict workflows.</li>
<li>Engineered managed Git worktrees, branch-aware Claude session resumption, streamed and persisted run events, and human diff review before delivery actions. Added handling for concurrent resolution pushes and remote branch changes. <a href="https://conorbrown.orangecastle.net/projects/mega-desk">Architecture case study</a>.</li>
<li>Authored <strong>CLAUDE.md conventions</strong> covering DDD, dependency boundaries, modern C#, and a reference vertical slice; reinforced standards through code reviews and workshops.</li>
<li>Reduced CI/CD duration from roughly <strong>40–60 minutes to 19 minutes</strong>; reduced core test execution from 8–9 minutes to approximately 21 seconds through coverage-tooling changes.</li>
<li>Built remote management infrastructure serving <strong>2,000+ servers</strong> and an Azure Service Bus usage-logging platform designed around a <strong>99.9% delivery SLA</strong>.</li>
</ul></section>
<section><h2>Professional experience</h2>
<h3>MIRATECH <span>April 2025–Present</span></h3><p class="role">Software Developer III · Architecture and platform leadership responsibilities</p><ul>
<li>Modernized a legacy .NET Framework MVC application to .NET 10; builds C#/ASP.NET Core Web APIs and React/TypeScript interfaces with SQL Server persistence.</li>
<li>Uses Claude Code in implementation, refactoring, testing, and legacy-code workflows; checks proposed changes against domain rules, architecture boundaries, tests, and review before delivery.</li>
<li>Guides engineers through design decisions and code reviews; led event-storming and DDD implementation sessions to make business rules and ownership explicit.</li>
<li>Implemented DDD/CQRS workflow and rule-builder capabilities across aggregates, APIs, persistence, UI, and end-to-end testing, while guiding architectural reviews and workshops.</li>
<li>Led a coordinated modernization path toward Azure App Service, including runtime configuration, Entra integration, Key Vault identity, parallel pipelines, staging validation, and rollback planning.</li>
<li>Supported a product-line transition involving catalog identity, component modeling, pricing, drawings, indexing, and administrative tooling.</li>
<li>Modernized CI/CD and test workflows, including Playwright-based regression coverage; codified engineering standards in a CLAUDE.md reference guide.</li>
</ul>
<h3>IXOPAY <span>June 2021–April 2025</span></h3><p class="role">Senior Software Engineer</p><ul>
<li>Built payment-related microservices including a containerized Card Account Updater to address subscription churn caused by expiring payment credentials.</li>
<li>Engineered asynchronous API usage telemetry with Azure Service Bus and a 99.9% delivery SLA for billing-related data.</li>
<li>Introduced integration-test infrastructure and secure runtime configuration patterns across cloud services.</li>
</ul>
<h3>MissGroup / Hostek <span>January 2014–June 2021</span></h3><p class="role">Software Engineer</p><ul>
<li>Rebuilt web-hosting management workflows with .NET Web APIs, React, and an orchestration/gateway layer.</li>
<li>Designed remote infrastructure and deployment tooling operating across 2,000+ Windows servers, including IIS, firewall, certificate, and service management.</li>
<li>Built secure credential management and remote access functionality supporting controlled sharing.</li>
</ul></section>
<section><h2>Technical breadth</h2><p><strong>Backend and architecture:</strong> C#, .NET Framework and .NET 10, ASP.NET Core / Web API, MVC, Entity Framework Core, DDD, CQRS, Clean Architecture, event-driven design, microservices and modular monoliths.</p><p><strong>Cloud and platform:</strong> Azure App Service, Azure Service Bus, Key Vault, App Configuration, Docker, Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions, observability.</p><p><strong>Product and data:</strong> Blazor WASM, React, TypeScript, React Native/Expo, SQL Server, PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, Cosmos DB, query/index tuning, Playwright, xUnit, NUnit, and integration testing.</p><p><strong>AI development:</strong> Claude Code, Claude Agent SDK, Codex CLI, custom agent tooling, CLAUDE.md context conventions, agent workflows, prompt context, code review and validation.</p></section>
<section><h2>Independent products and certification</h2><p><strong>Pathway:</strong> software engineering education platform · <strong>Theoria:</strong> interactive music education platform. See <a href="/projects">project walkthroughs</a>.</p><p><strong>Certified Scrum Developer</strong> — Scrum Alliance</p></section>
